{"title":"2016 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> has a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82364c4133ac9d84246adeb9045ab0369c177c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FA=FB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9f4cb8cd01ce230066f3ce5412abf38dc79b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=DC$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1cf3a489a4a75ba57664d86aa9382ebdbe4959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAB}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdb8a9795ba0241dfd42592e0da6b3ca3dfa9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=ED$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f4151f8ac9f951f798810698ab708d02e12795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408b1b1ac63afdc7c57374eb64a96a01ba86f11a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMXE$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616d05a6cb10d1b2c940889b98aa13157bd40ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD,FX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which each cell of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> table can be filled with one of the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb1d5bfa4f986caf50b27b765d697478594fe88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in such a way that:\n</p>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"5\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td valign=\"top\">\n<ul><li>in each row and each column, one third of the entries are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one third are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and one third are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; and</li>\n<li>in any diagonal, if the number of entries on the diagonal is a multiple of three, then one third of the entries are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one third are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and one third are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note.</b> The rows and columns of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> table are each labelled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in a natural order. Thus each cell corresponds to a pair of positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87e88f3e8b65d91e121a285a0b48256bd99f7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i,j \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, the table has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a9b50fb391724dad29de2f5524d731f3dd1ccc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> diagonals of two types. A diagonal of first type consists all cells <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" />  for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a058b5b38c16c64a07a6497271d636475625efde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i+j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> is a constant, and the diagonal of this second type consists all cells <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e738b4769cbbf393ad5140314a87e41cdc70480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i-j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> is constant.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81b4c602605db9fc8b423f072ec587d7a7799e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = A_1A_2 \\cdots A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" /> be a convex polygon in the plane. The vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c577b1273a48064eeabf22edf9ac2c101a737cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,\\dots, A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> have integer coordinates and lie on a circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. An odd positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is given such that the squares of the side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are integers divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e80582d50572c4ea84dc35d4cfa14e79f67957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2S$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> is an integer divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of positive integers is called <i>fragrant</i> if it contains at least two elements and each of its elements has a prime factor in common with at least one of the other elements.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714f5b771a077d689c1b2fb3ba01ad7be51e21c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=n^2+n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />.  What is the least possible positive integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that there exists a non-negative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096f4d31ced33c7d415ee4bcf54720b421c2f206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{P(a+1),P(a+2),\\ldots,P(a+b)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" /> is fragrant?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740a0adcfbdff44b7db27d0b8974a6369d9948d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)(x-2)\\cdots(x-2016)=(x-1)(x-2)\\cdots (x-2016)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>is written on the board, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> linear factors on each side. What is the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which it is possible to erase exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6395e1f759197dbcfc89b4990a2e34d913af689a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4032$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> linear factors so that at least one factor remains on each side and the resulting equation has no real solutions?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> line segments in the plane such that every two segments cross and no three segments meet at a point. Geoff has to choose an endpoint of each segment and place a frog on it facing the other endpoint. Then he will clap his hands <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> times. Every time he claps,each frog will immediately jump forward to the next intersection point on its segment. Frogs never change the direction of their jumps. Geoff wishes to place the frogs in such a way that no two of them will ever occupy the same intersection point at the same time.\n</p><p>(a) Prove that Geoff can always fulfill his wish if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.\n</p><p>(b) Prove that Geoff can never fulfill his wish if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO\" title=\"2016 IMO\">2016 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems\">2015 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems\">2017 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017124122\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 360/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 854/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11052/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.547      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.547      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17946:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017124122 and revision id 207971. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}